  "split": "V17 recording-disjoint 60/20/20 over all available RADIal recordings",
  "seed": 20261030,
  "rules": [
    "1. Recording-disjoint roles. Frames of one recording are strongly correlated in time, so frames of a recording never cross roles (as in the official RADIal / FFTRadNet sequence split, Rebut et al., CVPR 2022).",
    "2. TEST contains only recordings that never informed a design decision or an evaluation gate in V12-V16: recordings previously in TRAIN (used only to fit entropy models that are discarded and retrained here) and the newly added ones.",
    "3. VALIDATION = previous VALIDATION recordings plus FFTRadNet's own held-out recordings that are present, so FFTRadNet's unseen-recording check is kept.",
    "4. TEST is filled from the rule-2 pool by a seeded shuffle and greedy selection towards 20% of all cubes, with no single recording above 35% of TEST and at least 6 recordings, so recording-level confidence intervals stay meaningful.",
    "5. TRAIN = all remaining recordings (about 60%)."
  ],
